      <title>CloudBridges: bridging social networks</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Lightning Talks</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The talk will explain the underlying technology of Google&amp;#39;s OpenSocial platform, and the philosophy of DataPortability, then give an example of friending between two social network accounts via CloudBridges.  The future potential of a fully open, Social Web will be explored.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A CloudBridge is a small FOSS application you can install into your profile on a social network which provides you with a microformat-based profile on the open Web, with a controllable level of privacy.  It lets you specify which friends can see your profile, even if those friends are on a different social network.  As such it is the first public example of a meta social network, where people from different networks can friend each other without having to create any new accounts.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
